734	SWZ	GGXWDG	Eswatini	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	"Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: FY2022/23 Reporting in calendar year: No. Fiscal year data are mapped to calendar year as follows: FY(t/t+1) = CY(t) Start/end months of reporting year: April/March GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 2001 Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government Valuation of public debt: Nominal value Instruments included in gross and net debt: Loans; Securities Other than Shares Primary domestic currency: Swazi lilangeni Data last updated: 02/25/2025"	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	0.743	0.770	0.877	0.913	1.136	1.538	1.800	2.190	2.889	2.587	2.906	2.689	2.729	3.252	3.940	3.972	3.182	4.581	5.140	5.924	6.661	6.654	8.162	11.250	13.019	16.615	20.453	25.944	27.157	33.049	34.008	35.461	40.097	45.249	49.302	53.342	57.862	62.398	2023
