648	GMB	GGXWDG	The Gambia	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	"Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: 2023 Fiscal assumptions: The authorities are committed to keeping the 2024 fiscal framework anchored on the approved 2024 budget. The overall fiscal deficit target remains unchanged relative to the approved 2024 budget, at 2.7 percent of GDP. The other fiscal parameters also rema Reporting in calendar year: Yes Start/end months of reporting year: January/December GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 1986 Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government Valuation of public debt: Nominal value Instruments included in gross and net debt: Loans; Securities Other than Shares Primary domestic currency: Gambian dalasi Data last updated: 03/20/2025"	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	9.457	11.830	16.583	22.050	23.485	24.256	25.840	12.103	13.700	15.018	18.567	20.450	22.464	28.810	36.474	40.637	51.086	61.009	67.249	75.329	80.159	87.673	101.552	111.122	126.496	133.421	135.688	136.116	136.264	136.767	138.612	2023
