263	HTI	GGXWDG	Haiti	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: FY2023/24 Notes: General Government only includes Central Government due to data availability Reporting in calendar year: No. Fiscal year data are mapped to calendar year as follows: FY(t-1/t) = CY(t) Start/end months of reporting year: October/September GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 1986 Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government Valuation of public debt: Nominal value Primary domestic currency: Haitian gourde Data last updated: 03/18/2025	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	24.416	26.067	28.816	43.389	43.385	52.418	73.800	72.944	83.205	100.226	87.027	136.102	91.581	119.041	116.843	137.122	161.379	144.259	172.061	205.939	222.219	259.558	330.040	323.635	490.447	639.752	796.515	517.246	525.215	563.567	645.245	744.270	854.395	963.986	2024
