565	PLW	GGXWDG	Palau	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: FY2022/23 Reporting in calendar year: No. Fiscal year data are mapped to calendar year as follows: FY(t-1/t) = CY(t). Start/end months of reporting year: October/September GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 2001 Basis of recording: Accrual General government includes: Central Government Valuation of public debt: Face value Primary domestic currency: US dollar Data last updated: 04/14/2025	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	0.055	0.055	0.055	0.054	0.057	0.057	0.055	0.066	0.064	0.067	0.063	0.060	0.066	0.062	0.068	0.061	0.072	0.078	0.085	0.086	0.135	0.165	0.171	0.211	0.213	0.215	0.214	0.201	0.188	0.175	0.161	2023
