866	TON	GGXWDG	Tonga	General government gross debt	Gross debt consists of all liabilities that require payment or payments of interest and/or principal by the debtor to the creditor at a date or dates in the future. This includes debt liabilities in the form of SDRs, currency and deposits, debt securities, loans, insurance, pensions and standardized guarantee schemes, and other accounts payable. Thus, all liabilities in the GFSM 2001 system are debt, except for equity and investment fund shares and financial derivatives and employee stock options. Debt can be valued at current market, nominal, or face values (GFSM 2001, paragraph 7.110).	National currency	Billions	Source: Ministry of Finance or Treasury Latest actual data: FY2022/23 Reporting in calendar year: No. Fiscal year data are mapped to calendar year as follows: FY(t-1/t) = CY(t) Start/end months of reporting year: July/June GFS Manual used: Government Finance Statistics Manual (GFSM) 2014 Basis of recording: Cash General government includes: Central Government Valuation of public debt: Face value Primary domestic currency: Tongan pa'anga Data last updated: 04/10/2025	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	n/a	0.120	0.145	0.189	0.242	0.250	0.247	0.220	0.232	0.226	0.223	0.259	0.317	0.394	0.434	0.383	0.378	0.435	0.461	0.455	0.492	0.481	0.488	0.508	0.516	0.528	0.491	0.603	0.737	0.889	1.062	1.268	1.502	2023
